<title>PORTUGAL: Yield eases on Portuguese three-month bills.</title>
<headline>Yield eases on Portuguese three-month bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield eased to 6.4660 percent, from 6.5395 percent previously, at the Treasury's sale of 91-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Treasury placed 16.25 billion escudos of the 20 billion on offer. The last such sale was on November 29.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
